    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="IRS990ScheduleO" softwareId="24020490" softwareVersionNum="2024v5.2">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE BOARD OF THE SCOTTISH RITE CATHEDRAL OF SAN DIEGO, INC., WHOSE MEMBERS ARE ALSO THE FINANCE COMMITTEE OF THE ANCIENT AND ACCEPTED SCOTTISH RITE BODIES OF SAN DIEGO, REVIEWS FORM 990 TO THE EXTENT THAT IT AGREES TO THE REVIEWED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS BEFORE AN OFFICER SIGNS AND SUBMITS TO THE INTERNAL REVENUE SERVICE.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 12c</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>IN ORDER TO AVOID ANY CONFLICT OF INTEREST, THE EXISTENCE OF SUCH FINANCIAL INTEREST MUST BE DISCLOSED TO THE OTHER OFFICERS, TRUSTEES OR COMMITTEE MEMBERS PRESENT AND THE PERSON MUST, AFTER DISCUSSION OF THE TRANSACTION, REMOVE HIM/HERSELF FROM THE MEETING AND REFRAIN FROM VOTING ON THE TRANSACTION IN QUESTION. ANNUALLY, EACH OFFICER, TRUSTEE OR COMMITTEE MEMBER MUST DISCLOSE TO THE VALLEY'S PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE ANY FINANCIAL INTEREST THAT COULD GIVE RISE TO CONFLICTS OF INTEREST. EACH YEAR, THE VALLEY'S PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE SHALL AFFIRM IN WRITING TO THE ORIENT'S SGIG/DEPUTY THAT ALL DISCLOSURES HAVE BEEN MADE AND SHALL ALSO DISCLOSE ANY FINANCIAL INTEREST THAT HE/SHE, THE PERSONAL REPRESENTATIVE, MAY HAVE THAT COULD GIVE RISE TO CONFLICTS OF INTEREST. THERE WERE NO NOTED CONFLICTS OF INTEREST FOR THE YEAR ENDED DECEMBER 31, 2021.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section C, Line 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
